    "summary": "Root cause: the accepted decision lane.xi (JTG D60-2015 Table 4.3.1-5 transverse lane-load factor) was set to 0.78, but for 2 design lanes the applicable clause formula gives 1.0. This made the finished model violate the L2-1 consistency check (each member parameter must re-compute from its governing clause). It was not traceable to a suspect decision because it was a stale accepted value; re-writing the instance re-triggered the constraint layer, which withdrew lane.xi (and the dependent f1/lane.mu).\n\nRepair: re-proposed lane.xi = 1.0 (evidence JTGD60-4.3.1-xi, dec:lane.n_lanes), re-ran the modal analysis (f1 = 3.4017 Hz), then re-decided lane.mu = 0.1767·ln(f1) − 0.0157 = 0.20063 (JTGD60-4.3.2, fact:f1). Regenerated the model successfully.\n\nFinal model (F0/K2_r9/A08_model.py): 30 m single simply supported span, spine-beam 2D spine idealized, 3 precast prestressed small-box girders (C40, γ=26 kN/m³, A=3.4168 m², I=1.0648 m⁴, w=88.836 kN/m, m=9.0557 t/m), plain laminated elastomeric bearings at both abutments (6 per line, S=10.714, Kv=8.52e6 kN/m, Kh=18000 kN/m, vertical/longitudinal springs, rotation free). Highway Class II loading, 2 lanes: qk=7.875 kN/m, Pk=240 kN, ξ=1.0, μ=0.2006.\n\nResults: f1 = 3.402 Hz (next modes 13.49, 29.88 Hz); self-weight reactions 1332.55 + 1332.55 = 2665.09 kN = total self-weight; self-weight midspan moment 9994.1 kN·m; live-load max positive moment 6449.6 kN·m. All L1/L2/L3 checks pass."
